            <ArticleTitle>Sleep apnoea and nocturnal angina.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1085-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hypoxaemia occurs with sleep apnoea and might induce nocturnal angina. Sleep apnoea was found in 9 of 10 patients with nocturnal angina pectoris. Nocturnal angina diminished during treatment of sleep apnoea by continuous positive airway-pressure, and the number of nocturnal myocardial ischaemic events measured by computerised vector-cardiography was reduced.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
